definition outside the closure: the receiver's declared fields still validate each incoming message natively. Existing relate fan-in/copy proofs stay unchanged.\n\nDerive admits and captures the port's slot read in the handler's existing M8-owned program. It compares the verified sender's full ScopeRef with that fixed slot before handler effects. A different verified sender under the same pin returns guard-failed with reason not-the-sender, retaining one deciding entry and one result with zero handler effects as ruling99f628a5 requires. The existing source pin/under checks remain. Dependencies and explanations name the actual slot read; no declaration is reinterpreted at execution.\n\nPlease adopt this minimal at-slot extension, or specify the correction before I edit source. If it requires a new record form under kernel gate1bd7dde8, I will stop and file that design instead. No source edit, compiler, test, build, live room or deployment has run for M1a.","body":{"conditions":"Adopt or correct the existing receive-port at-slot extension, its static and native refusal behavior, before any M1a source edit.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}